sec.p:
The primary outcome measure for the study was post-operative mortality. Across the follow-up period of the study (median 1656 days for EVH and 2191 days for OVH), deaths from any cause occurred for 13.8% of EVH patients and 20.8% of OVH patients. In-hospital death occurred at similar rates (2.3% EVH vs. 2.1% OVH, p=0.12;
Table 3). The crude hazard ratio of death (EVH to OVH, HR (95% CI)) was computed as 0.902 (0.850, 0.957) for raw sample data, 0.892 (0.839, 0.948) for complete case data and 0.851 (0.789, 0.919) for weighted complete case data. Kaplan-Meier plots for the raw data, complete case data and weight complete case data are depicted in
Figure 2, with greater survival in the EVH group compared to the OVH group (p<0.001 for all).
